{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"surface","tool":"save_skill","arguments":{"name":"json_xs_pretty_print","content":"# Pretty-print JSON with json_xs\n\nUse when asked to indent compact JSON using the sandboxed json_xs program.\n\nRun run_program with args [\"-f\", \"json\", \"-t\", \"json-pretty\"] and the exact JSON text as stdin. The -p flag is unsupported.\n\nCheck exit is 0 and stderr is empty. Verify stdout is valid JSON with the same object structure, keys, array order, and values as the input, and contains line breaks and indentation. Return stdout verbatim when an exact result is requested.\n\nVerified example: input {\"user\":{\"profile\":{\"tags\":[\"admin\",\"dev\"]}}} followed by newline produces nested multiline JSON with three spaces per indentation level and preserves both tags in order."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
